add('electron-ohos-hardware-shortcut-modifier-replay','Replay hardware shortcuts when the OH Electron runtime drops modifiers','input',['electron'],
 'Track Control, Alt and Shift from their own key events in the main process, cancel the plain key that arrives while one is held, and replay it through webContents.sendInputEvent with explicit modifiers.',
 'On a PC keyboard Ctrl+A inserts a letter or triggers a plain-key action, Ctrl+C/V/Z/S do nothing, and the page sees ctrlKey=false although the Ctrl key itself produced keydown and keyup.',
 'Electron on OH with hardware keyboards, where the selected runtime forwards the modifier keys but not their flags on the following key. This describes one reviewed runtime generation, so confirm the symptom before installing the bridge; keep it behind process.platform === \'openharmony\'.',
 'Ctrl+A|keyboard shortcut|modifier|ctrlKey false|before-input-event|sendInputEvent|hardware keyboard|AppGallery review',
 ['electron-ohos-platform-capability-gates','qt-ohos-terminal-direct-key-input','electron-ohos-window-types'],
 ['Log before-input-event for Ctrl+A. Install the bridge only when input.control is false on the letter while a separate Control keyDown was seen.',
  'On app web-contents-created, attach before-input-event per webContents and keep per-contents state for Control, Alt, Shift and the replayed keys.',
  'For a Control/Alt/Shift event, record state from input.type and let it through. Ignore keyDown events that already carry input.control, input.alt or input.meta so replayed events and a fixed runtime pass untouched.',
  'For a plain keyDown while Control or Alt is held, map input.code to an Electron keyCode (KeyA to A, Digit1 to 1, ArrowUp to Up, and so on), call event.preventDefault(), remember the mapping by code and call contents.sendInputEvent({type: \'keyDown\', keyCode, modifiers}).',
  'On the matching keyUp, cancel it and replay keyUp with the same keyCode and modifiers, so a held key never sticks.',
  'Reset modifier state and pending replays on browser-window-blur, because a modifier released in another window never reaches this one.'],
 'This is a compatibility bridge for a runtime defect, not an input API contract. Unmapped codes pass through unchanged. Meta is not tracked in the reviewed bridge, and IME composition and key-repeat behavior were not reviewed. Prefer a runtime that delivers flags if one is available.',
 'Replaying without the already-has-modifier guard loops or double-fires. Forgetting keyUp replay leaves stuck keys. Skipping the blur reset leaves Ctrl logically held after Alt+Tab, turning later typing into shortcuts. Registering a global hotkey instead captures keys from other apps.',
 'With a physical keyboard, or injected device-level events if your tool can send Ctrl, test Ctrl+A/C/V/Z/Y/S and Ctrl+Shift+Z on the canvas and in a text field, then press Ctrl, switch app, release and return. Confirm no shortcut fires while another app is in front and that plain typing still works.',
 [('drawio-in-harmony','application/src/main/harmony-runtime.js'),('drawio-in-harmony','application/src/main/electron.js'),('drawio-in-harmony','RELEASE.md')],
 reports=['The source release notes report a device regression with uinput-injected keys on one 2in1 product (HAD-W24). Attributed report; not repeated here.'])
add('electron-ohos-asar-store-precheck','Ship the OH Electron payload as app.asar to clear source-file checks','packaging',['electron'],
 'Pack the application into one resources/app.asar with the upstream builder file exclusions instead of loose resfile sources, and fail the build if any source file remains in the HAP.',
 'Store pre-review warns that the package must not contain source files, and the HAP holds thousands of loose .js files under resources/resfile/resources/app.',
 'Electron OH hosts whose runtime accepts --app-path pointing at an asar. Store policy and check wording belong to the distribution channel and can change. Native addons and files opened by path may need to stay outside the archive.',
 'app.asar|asar|source files in package|软件包中不应包含源码文件|resfile|AGC pre-review|AppGallery',
 ['electron-ohos-builder-packaging','electron-ohos-resfile-injection','electron-ohos-native-addon-abi'],
 ['Apply the desktop build\'s asar and files configuration to the OH staging step, so development sources, source maps and test assets are excluded for the same reasons as on desktop.',
  'Write the payload to resources/app.asar. Keep only files that must remain loose, such as license texts, next to it and remove the old loose app directory so a stale tree cannot be packaged.',
  'Check that the host starts Electron with the asar as its app path, and that any code that resolves files under __dirname still works inside the archive.',
  'Add a build check that lists HAP entries and rejects .js, .ts and similar source extensions outside the archive.',
  'Record the asar digest in the build manifest so a rebuilt package can be compared with what was validated.'],
 'An asar is packaging, not protection: its contents remain readable. Native .node files cannot be loaded from inside an archive without unpack support; see the addon and load-location entries. The reviewed staging script writes the archive itself to avoid a dependency, and the standard asar tool is an equally valid choice.',
 'Adding app.asar while leaving the loose tree still fails the check. Dropping the upstream exclusion list ships development sources inside the archive. Assuming the check is cleared without re-running pre-review.',
 'Unzip the built HAP and search for source extensions outside app.asar. Start the app cold and exercise file-relative features such as templates, printing and shape libraries, then re-run the store pre-review.',
 [('drawio-in-harmony','scripts/stage-drawio-application.mjs'),('drawio-in-harmony','scripts/verify-probe-hap.ps1'),('drawio-in-harmony','RELEASE.md')],
 reports=['The source release notes report that the rebuilt package starts with --app-path=.../app.asar on a device. Whether the store check cleared is not established by the reviewed files.'])
add('electron-ohos-platform-binding-loader-shim','Provide the missing OH platform package behind a Node native-binding loader','native-addon',['electron'],
 'When a package selects its addon through an optional per-platform package that has no openharmony-arm64 release, materialize that package at build time and bypass any product check your self-built addon cannot pass.',
 'The window stays about:blank and the log reports No usable native binding found for ...-openharmony-arm64, or native binding product mismatch: expected X, got openharmony-arm64, even though the .node file loads.',
 'Electron OH apps depending on npm packages that resolve prebuilt bindings by platform/arch package name. Reviewed for one internal-API addon under Node 22.17 / Node-API 10 with a self-built napi-v9 binding. The shim bypasses a validation step, so it is only appropriate for an addon you build and verify yourself.',
 'No usable native binding found|native binding product mismatch|openharmony-arm64|optional platform package|about:blank|pnpm deploy|custom loader',
 ['electron-ohos-native-addon-abi','native-code-load-location','electron-ohos-older-runtime-shims'],
 ['Read the loader to learn the package name it requires and what it validates. Unpublished platform packages are absent after pnpm deploy, so the failure appears only at runtime.',
  'At collect time, create node_modules/<package>-openharmony-arm64 with package.json, lib/index.js and prebuilt/<addon>.node, using the addon built for the OH ABI. Fail the build if that binary is missing.',
  'If the loader rejects your binding because of self-reported metadata, either make the addon report what the loader expects, or replace the wrapper package entry with a re-export of the platform package. Keep the same exported API.',
  'Place the same .node where the OH linker namespace can reach it, such as the HAP native libs directory; a copy under the app files sandbox is not dlopen-able in the reviewed environment.',
  'Pin the upstream package version and repeat the check when it changes, since each regeneration of node_modules removes the shim.'],
 'Prefer an upstream openharmony package or a matching product field when you control the addon: the wrapper replacement also removes the upstream availability check. The addon\'s ABI still has to match the runtime; see the addon ABI entry.',
 'Treating the about:blank window as a renderer problem instead of a boot failure in the main process. Shipping the shim without the libs copy, leaving the addon unloadable. Applying a re-export to a package whose exports differ per platform.',
 'After a clean collect, confirm the platform package and the wrapper shim exist in the packaged tree, the loader resolves each exported function on the device, and the host boots with a visible window. Repeat after updating the upstream package.',
 [('dsh-desktop-hos','scripts/collect-dsh.mjs')],
 reports=['The source commit reports that all internal loader APIs resolved and the host booted on a device. Attributed report; not repeated here.'])
add('native-self-extract-gnu-long-names','Handle GNU tar long names when self-extracting a runtime payload','packaging',[],
 'A first-run extractor for a payload written by GNU tar must apply typeflag L long-name entries to the following entry and skip K payloads, or it will truncate paths at 100 bytes.',
 'First-run payload extraction aborts with EISDIR after creating a directory with a name cut at 100 characters, and the app then fails to find a deep dependency and shows a blank window.',
 'Apps that ship a tar payload and unpack it with a small custom parser into the OH sandbox because no system tar is relied on. The tar format detail is general; it matters on OH because such extractors are written by hand for this purpose.',
 'tar|GNU long name|typeflag L|././@LongLink|EISDIR|100 byte|payload extraction|first run|node_modules',
 ['native-dependency-closure','startup-work-prerequisites','sandbox-paths-and-app-identity'],
 ['Read the 512-byte ustar header and keep the typeflag rather than classifying everything except files and directories as skippable.',
  'For typeflag L, read its data as the real name of the next entry, removing the trailing NUL. Apply it after the same path normalization used for ordinary names.',
  'For typeflag K, consume the data. Handle or explicitly reject pax x/g headers and links, depending on what your archive producer can emit.',
  'Validate the resulting path stays inside the destination before writing.',
  'Fail the whole extraction visibly and leave no ready marker when any entry fails, so the next launch retries instead of booting a partial tree.'],
 'Using a bundled, tested tar library avoids the whole class. Alternatively have the build produce pax or restrict path length, but node_modules trees regularly exceed 100 bytes.',
 'Counting a partial extract as success. Testing only with short paths. Treating the L payload as a file named ././@LongLink.',
 'Build a payload containing paths over 100 and over 255 bytes, extract in the sandbox, compare the file count and digests with the source tree, and kill the app mid-extraction to confirm the next launch recovers.',
 [('dsh-desktop-hos','src-main/tar-extract.js')],
 limitations=['The reviewed parser skips links and pax headers by design because its archive does not contain them; path containment and the failure marker steps are curator additions drawn from general practice, not observed in this file.'],
 reports=['The source commit reports extraction previously aborting after 13,653 of 43,555 files. Attributed report.'])
add('napi-handle-scope-without-js-frame','Open a handle scope around Node-API work outside a JS call frame','native-bridge',[],
 'Native code that runs from a uv_async or other event-loop callback has no default handle scope, so wrap each call that creates napi_values in an RAII handle scope.',
 'ArkTS strings and closures grow steadily across page entries and GC never reclaims them; heap snapshots show objects retained through a local handle root, and views passed to native code leak.',
 'Node-API on the ArkTS runtime, called from native tasks posted to the main loop rather than from a JS-invoked native method. Applies to any framework bridge using this path.',
 'napi_open_handle_scope|napi_close_handle_scope|uv_async|handle leak|LocalHandleRoot|ArkTS memory leak|heap snapshot|RAII',
 ['napi-thread-and-handle-lifetime','native-event-loop-handle-teardown','kmp-napi-string-allocator-ownership'],
 ['List native entry points by how they are entered: a native method called from JS already has a scope, but a uv_async callback, timer or posted main-thread task does not.',
  'Create a small RAII type that opens a scope in its constructor, records whether that succeeded, and closes it in its destructor. Delete copy operations.',
  'Declare it at the top of each scope-less function, before the first napi_value is created, so every early return closes it.',
  'Search for unpaired napi_open_handle_scope calls and convert them. Any value needed after the scope ends must become a napi_ref.',
  'For long loops creating many values in one call, add a nested scope per iteration.'],
 'This complements the thread and lifetime rule: that entry covers which thread and reference to use, and this one covers when local handles get released. Do not open a scope on a thread that does not own the env.',
 'Returning a napi_value created inside a scope you close first. Opening a scope manually and missing an early-return path. Assuming GC can collect objects still held by handles from an unclosed scope.',
 'Repeat the page or feature entry and exit many times, let the app idle, and compare object counts in heap snapshots. String and closure counts should stop growing with the round count, and callbacks should still receive valid values.',
 [('kuiklyui',K+'utils/KRNapiHandleScope.h'),('kuiklyui',K+'manager/KRArkTSManager.cpp'),('kuiklyui',K+'expand/components/forward/KRForwardArkTSView.cpp')],
 reports=['The source commit reports a 50-round page-entry heap comparison on a device. Attributed report; not repeated here.'])
add('native-arkui-callback-no-throw-text','Keep text conversion from throwing inside ArkUI node event callbacks','input',[],
 'Cap pasted text on a UTF-8 character boundary and use replacing decoders in ArkUI node event paths, because a C++ exception escaping the callback terminates the process.',
 'Pasting long text into a length-limited native input crashes with SIGABRT, often only when the limit is counted in characters and the pasted text is multi-byte.',
 'Native C++ text handling on OH_ArkUI_NodeEvent callbacks. PC boundary: large clipboard pastes from a keyboard are routine, so the limit path is reached more often than with touch input.',
 'paste crash|SIGABRT|OH_ArkUI_NodeEvent|UTF-8 truncation|std::range_error|wstring_convert|maxLength|U+FFFD',
 ['native-unicode-selection-boundaries','utf8-command-payload-transport','native-arkui-node-attribute-api-guard'],
 ['Find byte-based caps such as min(strlen(text), maxLength * 4). They are acceptable as copy limits only if they end on a character boundary.',
  'Step back from the cut over UTF-8 continuation bytes, at most three, and drop a final sequence that the cut left incomplete.',
  'Replace throwing conversions such as std::wstring_convert with decoders that substitute U+FFFD for ill-formed input, and use one replacement rule in each direction.',
  'Do semantic length limiting afterwards, on the decoded text, in the filter that knows whether the limit counts bytes, characters or visual width.',
  'Treat the C callback boundary as no-throw. Catch at the outermost handler when called code might still throw.'],
 'Replacement changes text only when the input is ill-formed; legitimate text is untouched. Where data integrity matters more than continuity, return an explicit error instead, still without throwing across the callback.',
 'Fixing only the truncation leaves any other ill-formed source able to crash the app. Fixing only the decoder hides truncation as replacement characters in the input.',
 'Paste strings of CJK, emoji and invalid byte sequences at limits that fall inside a multi-byte character, using byte, character and visual-width limit modes. Expect no crash, no partial character and correct length handling.',
 [('kuiklyui',K+'utils/KRUtfUtil.cpp'),('kuiklyui',K+'utils/KRUtfUtil.h'),('kuiklyui',K+'expand/components/input/KRTextFieldView.cpp')])
add('native-custom-text-app-font-scale-cap','Apply the app font-scale cap in custom-drawn text','text',[],
 'Text a native renderer scales itself must use the smaller of Configuration.fontSizeScale and UIContext.getMaxFontScale, since the configuration value is the raw system setting without the app cap.',
 'With a large system font size, ArkUI text in the app stops growing at the declared limit, but text drawn by a native paragraph or custom renderer keeps growing and breaks layout.',
 'Apps whose renderer multiplies a scale in native code instead of letting ArkUI scale text, with a cap from app.json5 configuration fontSizeMaxScale or UIContext.setMaxFontScale. getMaxFontScale is API 13+. Check at PC window sizes, where users commonly raise display and font settings.',
 'fontSizeScale|fontSizeMaxScale|setMaxFontScale|getMaxFontScale|font scale|Configuration|custom text renderer|KRParagraph',
 ['text-weight-versus-scale-policy','arkui-density-and-inset-layout','native-arkui-node-attribute-api-guard'],
 ['Identify which text ArkUI scales and which your renderer scales. Only the second needs this.',
  'At initialization compute min(config.fontSizeScale, uiContext.getMaxFontScale()) and pass that to the native side.',
  'Apply the same calculation in the onConfigurationUpdated path so changing the setting at runtime keeps the cap.',
  'Guard getMaxFontScale with try/catch, or a null UIContext check, and fall back to no extra cap on older APIs.',
  'Keep an existing app-level follow-system switch separate; when it is off the scale stays 1.'],
 'The reviewed comment notes getMaxFontScale reports a default of 2.0 when no cap is configured, with a range of 1 to 3, so this also changes behavior for apps that declared nothing. Verify on your target API.',
 'Fixing only the initial value so runtime changes break the cap. Applying the cap on the native side as well, which is harmless for min but duplicates the source of truth.',
 'Set the system font scale above and below the app cap, both before launch and while running, and compare native-drawn text with an ArkUI Text at the same size.',
 [('kuiklyui','core-render-ohos/src/main/ets/KRNativeRenderController.ets')])
add('kmp-kuikly-ohos-sync-gesture-context-scheduling','Run KuiklyUI context tasks on the main thread during sync gestures','input',['kotlin-multiplatform'],
 'During a synchronous touchMove or scroll session on OH, pause the context thread and drain its queue on the main thread in 2 ms slices, so the sync event does not wait out a full frame task.',
 'Dragging or scrolling a KuiklyUI page with sync events on OH janks because each main-thread sync callback blocks on the context thread lock while frame tasks run.',
 'KuiklyUI on OH from the renderer generation with sync-event sessions, with sync touchMove or syncScroll registered. This is a scheduling change inside the renderer, so prefer upgrading to reimplementing it. Pointer dragging on PC exercises the same continuous sync path.',
 'sync touchMove|syncScroll|context thread|main-thread freeze|jank|vsync|input-first|KRThread|2ms',
 ['kmp-kuikly-ohos-resize-sync','kmp-kuikly-statusbar-scroll-ownership','rendering-budget-and-progressive-ui'],
 ['Bound a session from ArkUI state: first pointer down to last pointer up or cancel for touch, and scroll start to scroll stop including inertia and animated offsets. Single-shot events such as keyboard height changes do not open one.',
  'Reference-count sessions, make repeated starts for the same view and event idempotent, and release them when a view is removed, destroyed or an ancestor stops the event.',
  'Have the context thread release its task lock after the current task when the main thread is waiting, returning the rest of the batch to the front of its queue.',
  'While a session is active, run context tasks on the main thread for at most 2 ms per round, and postpone UI work posted while the context task lock is held.',
  'Let frame tasks wait for the current input and merge at most one vsync. Keep the deferred frame per page and drop it when the page is destroyed.'],
 'A long-running single task is not interrupted by the 2 ms budget. The reviewed spec also sets a nativeBuild gate choosing between vsync and a 12 ms timer for Compose, so a mismatched host and shared library version can change the path.',
 'Ending the session on the wrong event, such as finger up during inertia. Keeping one global deferred frame across pages. Delivering a stored frame to a destroyed page.',
 'Drag and fling long lists with heavy frame tasks while recording main-thread wait time and frame intervals. Interrupt the gesture, nest scrollers, and destroy the page in mid-gesture to confirm session counts return to zero.',
 [('kuiklyui','openspec/specs/ohos-sync-event-scheduling/spec.md'),('kuiklyui','openspec/specs/ohos-vsync-frame-dispatcher/spec.md'),('kuiklyui',K+'core/KRRenderCore.cpp')],
 limitations=['Requirements were read from the repository specification with renderer file changes sampled, not a line-by-line implementation audit.'])
add('native-avcodec-native-buffer-format','Read the OH native buffer format instead of the AVCodec NV12 alias','media',[],
 'Determine decoded pixel layout from OH_NativeBuffer_GetConfig, because AVCodec metadata can report NV12 for a 10-bit P010 buffer on some devices.',
 '10-bit (Main10) hardware-decoded video shows corrupted, half-width or wrongly colored frames in a buffer-mode pipeline, while 8-bit plays correctly.',
 'OH AVCodec buffer-mode decoding where the app copies or interprets frames itself, on devices that report the alias. Surface-mode playback that the system composes does not read these bytes. Display HDR capability is a separate question.',
 'P010|NV12|NV12_10bit|Main10|OH_NativeBuffer_GetConfig|OH_AVBuffer_GetNativeBuffer|stride|10-bit video|AVCodec',
 ['hdr-output-surface-and-capability','video-surface-backend-contract','flutter-native-video-output-selection'],
 ['Get the native buffer for each output with OH_AVBuffer_GetNativeBuffer, and read format and stride through OH_NativeBuffer_GetConfig.',
  'Map the native format explicitly: the reviewed code treats 24 as NV12 and 35 as P010, and uses metadata only when no native format is available. Return an error for other combinations.',
  'Use the byte stride and two bytes per sample when copying P010 rows, and calculate luma and chroma row bytes with overflow checks.',
  'Pass the real format downstream, such as AV_PIX_FMT_P010LE, so renderers and converters do not process 16-bit samples as 8-bit.',
  'Validate each plane size against stride and height before copying, then log the format that was resolved.'],
 'Constant values come from the reviewed bindings; confirm them against your SDK headers rather than copying numbers. If only 8-bit output is required, request a format conversion from the decoder where supported.',
 'Branching only on the metadata pixel format. Assuming stride equals width. Silently treating an unknown format as NV12.',
 'Play 8-bit and Main10 samples on each target device in buffer mode, compare colors and geometry with a reference frame, and confirm the log shows the resolved format. Include odd dimensions.',
 [('liberika','crates/erika/src/ohos/pixel_layout.rs'),('liberika','crates/erika/src/ohos/avcodec.rs')])
add('native-bridge-weak-optional-runtime-symbol','Bind a newer runtime symbol weakly in an OH native bridge','native-bridge',[],
 'Declare an optional API added to a separately shipped native runtime as a weak symbol and test it for null before use, so the bridge still loads against older runtimes.',
 'A bridge .so built against a newer header fails to load with an undefined symbol on older runtime libraries, disabling every feature for the sake of one optional call.',
 'C or C++ bridges on OH linked against a native library versioned or delivered separately from the bridge. Applies to direct dynamic linking; dlopen/dlsym consumers already have their own lookup. Linker settings that reject undefined symbols must be checked.',
 '#pragma weak|weak symbol|undefined symbol|version skew|optional API|native runtime compatibility|dlopen',
 ['ffi-library-and-symbol-availability','native-packaging-single-producer','native-dependency-closure'],
 ['Limit this to additive, optional functions. Compatibility-breaking ABI changes need a version check instead.',
  'Add #pragma weak symbol_name after the declaration, or an equivalent attribute, in the bridge translation unit.',
  'Before each call test the symbol address, and return a typed unsupported error naming the required update.',
  'Add a test that links the bridge against a stub runtime lacking the symbol, to catch accidental hard references, including from any other translation unit.',
  'Expose capability to the caller so the UI can hide the feature rather than failing when it is used.'],
 'Weak references only help if the final link tolerates them and the dynamic loader resolves them to null; verify on the target toolchain and device. Prefer a single versioned package when you control both libraries.',
 'Marking the symbol weak in one translation unit and calling it unguarded elsewhere. Using this to hide mismatched struct layouts between versions.',
 'Load the bridge with old and new runtime libraries on a device. Core playback or other base features must work with the old one, and the optional call must return the unsupported error instead of crashing.',
 [('liberika','packages/erika_ohos/src/main/cpp/presenter_bridge.h'),('liberika','packages/erika_flutter/ohos/tests/presenter_stub.cpp')])
add('native-wgpu-gles-adapter-limits','Clamp wgpu GLES device limits to what the OH adapter reports','rendering',[],
 'On the GL backend, request the smaller of the baseline limit and the adapter limit, because a reduced value can make device creation fail even though the renderer does not need the difference.',
 'Native renderer initialization returns no player or device after Vulkan is unavailable, with request_device reporting that limit max_compute_workgroups_per_dimension value 65535 is better than allowed 33778.',
 'Rust wgpu renderers on OH falling back to GLES. The reported values come from an x86_64 emulator on one host GPU; physical PC GPU limits were not established. Relevant to PC adaptation mainly because the emulator is a common test target.',
 'wgpu|GLES|request_device|max_compute_workgroups_per_dimension|emulator|downlevel_defaults|Vulkan unavailable|device limits',
 ['capability-gated-backend-initialization','rust-bridge-target-and-packaging','rendering-budget-and-progressive-ui'],
 ['Log the adapter backend and limits before requesting a device.',
  'Start from the baseline, and on Backend::Gl set each limit your shaders do not depend on to the minimum of the baseline and adapter values.',
  'Check that actual dispatch counts and shader varyings fit the reduced limits, rather than only passing device creation.',
  'Leave other backends\' requests unchanged, and add a unit test with the reported limit values.'],
 'If your workload really needs a higher limit, disable that feature or fail clearly instead. A driver crash under repeated create and destroy on the host, reported in the source investigation, remains unexplained and is not addressed by this change.',
 'Requesting adapter limits wholesale on every backend. Treating emulator success as evidence for a device GPU.',
 'Create a device and render on the emulator and on real hardware with both backends available and with Vulkan unavailable. Log the granted limits and repeat creation and destruction.',
 [('liberika','crates/erika/src/renderer/wgpu.rs'),('liberika','docs/investigations/ohos-gles-20261103/README.zh.md')],
 reports=['The source investigation reports HarmonyOS 5.1.0 / API 18 / x86_64 emulator playback after the fix, and an unexplained host driver crash during consecutive stress runs. Attributed report; not repeated here.'])
extend('ffi-library-and-symbol-availability',[('kuiklyui',K+'scheduler/KRContextScheduler.cpp')],'Added hidden-visibility export note from a release-only missing-symbol fix.',
 '**Release-only missing symbols.** A public C function can disappear from the dynamic symbol table when release builds use -fvisibility=hidden and strip. Mark the function with the library\'s export macro, then check the stripped release artifact, not just the debug build, with an `nm -D` style listing.')
GH='react-native-harmony-gesture-handler/harmony/gesture_handler/src/main/cpp/'
extend('rnoh-gesture-scroll-frame-hold',[('rnoh-gesture-handler',GH+'native/NativeGestureManagerScroll.cpp'),('rnoh-gesture-handler',GH+'NativeGestureManager.h')],'Added attach-before-mount retry note from a follow-up commit in the same gesture adapter.',
 '**Attach before mount.** RNOH creates a component before mounting it, so an attach can land before the view is inserted up to the surface root and find no ancestor scrollers to guard. Report that case as incomplete and retry on a short, bounded delay, looking the handler up again by tag on each attempt, instead of assuming the first scan was complete.')
